PRINT "Step 2 of 3: Set up Markdown converter (adf)."

DO Select the repository from @options.repository, otherwise vinod-rightmo/inux.
    Resolve the binary path as bin/adf-<os>-<arch> using @platform, with .exe on
    Windows. Use @options.adf_ref when supplied, otherwise the repository's
    default branch. Return an object with repository, path, and ref. AS package

DO Install @host.adf as one bounded transaction under @install_rules. Use verified
    @host.gh api with separate arguments --method, GET, --header,
    "Accept: application/vnd.github.raw+json", and the endpoint
    repos/<repository>/contents/<path> from @package. For an explicit ref, pass
    --raw-field with ref=<ref>. Stream raw stdout directly into a file in a unique
    private temporary directory; never print or text-decode the binary. Require
    the download to succeed before installation. Set executable permissions and
    run this binary with a small UTF-8 Markdown fixture and a separate .adf output
    file. Require valid ADF representing the fixture and an unchanged input.
    Compare the verified binary bytes with any installed copy; retain an identical
    copy or replace it at @host.adf. Preserve a working installation on failure.
    Clean only this transaction's temporary files on success or failure. Return
    an object with path, ready TRUE, and Boolean updated. AS converter

PRINT Report the verified converter path @converter.path and whether it was updated.
